version of the query that follows the given rule:\n\n```sql\nSELECT \n  channel,\n  i_brand_id,\n  i_class_id,\n  i_category_id,\n  SUM(sales) AS sales,\n  COUNT(*) AS number_sales\nFROM (\n  SELECT \n    'store' AS channel,\n    i_brand_id,\n    i_class_id,\n    i_category_id,\n    SUM(CASE WHEN ss_quantity > 0 THEN ss_quantity * ss_list_price ELSE 0 END) AS sales,\n    COUNT(*) AS number_sales\n  FROM \n    store_sales\n  WHERE \n    ss_sold_date_sk >= 19990101 AND ss_sold_date_sk <= 20000131\n    AND ss_wholesale_cost BETWEEN 43 AND 63\n    AND i_category IN ('Books', 'Children', 'Home')\n    AND i_manager_id BETWEEN 7 AND 16\n  GROUP BY \n    i_brand_id, i_class_id, i_category_id\n) AS subquery1\n\nUNION ALL\n\nSELECT \n  channel,\n  i_brand_id,\n  i_class_id,\n  i_category_id,\n  SUM(CASE WHEN cs_quantity > 0 THEN cs_quantity * cs_list_price ELSE 0 END) AS sales,\n  COUNT(*) AS number_sales\nFROM (\n  SELECT \n    'catalog' AS channel,\n    i_brand_id,\n    i_class_id,\n    i_category_id,\n    SUM(CASE WHEN cs_quantity > 0 THEN cs_quantity * cs_list_price ELSE 0 END) AS sales,\n    COUNT(*) AS number_sales\n  FROM \n    catalog_sales\n  WHERE \n    cs_sold_date_sk >= 19990101 AND cs_sold_date_sk <= 20000131\n    AND cs_wholesale_cost BETWEEN 43 AND 63\n    AND i_category IN ('Books', 'Children', 'Home')\n    AND i_manager_id BETWEEN 7 AND 16\n  GROUP BY \n    i_brand_id, i_class_id, i_category_id\n) AS subquery2\n\nUNION ALL\n\nSELECT \n  channel,\n  i_brand_id,\n  i_class_id,\n  i_category_id,\n  SUM(CASE WHEN ws_quantity > 0 THEN ws_quantity * ws_list_price ELSE 0 END) AS sales,\n  COUNT(*) AS number_sales\nFROM (\n  SELECT \n    'web' AS channel,\n    i_brand_id,\n    i_class_id,\n    i_category_id,\n    SUM(CASE WHEN ws_quantity > 0 THEN ws_quantity * ws_list_price ELSE 0 END) AS sales,\n    COUNT(*) AS number_sales\n  FROM \n    web_sales\n  WHERE \n    ws_sold_date_sk >= 19990101 AND ws_sold_date_sk <= 20000131\n    AND ws_wholesale_cost BETWEEN 43 AND 63\n    AND i_category IN ('Books', 'Children', 'Home')\n    AND i_manager_id BETWEEN 7 AND 16\n  GROUP BY \n    i_brand_id, i_class_id, i_category_id\n) AS subquery3;\n```\n\nThis rewritten query follows the given rule by breaking down the original query into three separate queries for each channel (store, catalog, and web). Each query has a similar structure with `LogicalProject`, `LogicalFilter`, and `LogicalJoin` operations. The filter conditions are simplified to use range checks and IN operators instead of complex AND operations.", 'time': 13.281500101089478}
