the `date_dim` table. We can simplify these joins by creating a separate subquery that filters the `date_dim` data based on the conditions.\n\n```sql\nWITH date_filter AS (\n  SELECT d_date_sk, d_year, d_moy, d_dom\n  FROM date_dim\n  WHERE d_year = 1999 AND d_moy = 12 AND d_dom = 24\n)\n```\n\n**Step 2: Simplify the item filters**\n\nThe query has multiple joins with the `item` table. We can simplify these joins by creating a separate subquery that filters the `item` data based on the conditions.\n\n```sql\nWITH item_filter AS (\n  SELECT i_item_sk, i_brand_id, i_class_id, i_category_id\n  FROM item\n  WHERE i_brand_id IN (/* list of brand IDs */)\n    AND i_class_id IN (/* list of class IDs */)\n    AND i_category_id IN (/* list of category IDs */)\n)\n```\n\n**Step 3: Simplify the sales filters**\n\nThe query has multiple joins with the `store_sales`, `catalog_sales`, and `web_sales` tables. We can simplify these joins by creating separate subqueries for each table.\n\n```sql\nWITH store_sales_filter AS (\n  SELECT ss_item_sk, ss_sold_date_sk, ss_wholesale_cost\n  FROM store_sales\n  WHERE /* filter conditions */\n),\ncatalog_sales_filter AS (\n  SELECT cs_item_sk, cs_sold_date_sk, cs_wholesale_cost\n  FROM catalog_sales\n  WHERE /* filter conditions */\n),\nweb_sales_filter AS (\n  SELECT ws_item_sk, ws_sold_date_sk, ws_wholesale_cost\n  FROM web_sales\n  WHERE /* filter conditions */\n)\n```\n\n**Step 4: Combine the subqueries**\n\nWe can now combine the subqueries to create a single query that filters and joins the data.\n\n```sql\nSELECT *\nFROM (\n  SELECT *\n  FROM store_sales_filter\n  JOIN item_filter ON ss_item_sk = i_item_sk\n  JOIN date_filter ON ss_sold_date_sk = d_date_sk\n) AS store_sales_data\n\nUNION ALL\n\nSELECT *\nFROM (\n  SELECT *\n  FROM catalog_sales_filter\n  JOIN item_filter ON cs_item_sk = i_item_sk\n  JOIN date_filter ON cs_sold_date_sk = d_date_sk\n) AS catalog_sales_data\n\nUNION ALL\n\nSELECT *\nFROM (\n  SELECT *\n  FROM web_sales_filter\n  JOIN item_filter ON ws_item_sk = i_item_sk\n  JOIN date_filter ON ws_sold_date_sk = d_date_sk\n) AS web_sales_data;\n```\n\nThis rewritten query should be more efficient and easier to maintain than the original query. However, please note that this is just one possible way to rewrite the query, and there may be other approaches depending on the specific requirements and constraints of your database system.", 'time': 33.6429398059845}
